Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 21:44:28 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1124/1286] The page in Ukrainian and Belarusian, whole (1166,
 part three)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- heresy-i18n-uk.js, heresy-i18n-be.js: every key of the Russian catalog (2429), built by
  build_tr_cat.py from the translators' tables; plural forms one/few/many/other; no word of
  the root «роб/раб».
- Numbers and dates in the page's language (RuachI18n.locales): 24 576 in Russian, 24,576 in
  English. Belarusian borrows Russian's formats (Chrome has no Belarusian dates); in the Writer
  its dates go numeric, so no Russian month names show.
- {#N} takes a number grouped by plain spaces too (the no-break space of 24 576 is a plain one
  after norm()), and its plural reads it whole.
- The recaps of kit/loras/sources.json (the sliders' and each LoRA's about) translated in their tips.
- Russian: the fonts button named as it is, «Какую DAW ты используешь?», «чекпоинт раз в {8}».

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
